{"name":"Traditional Blue","hex":"#1f648d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"traditional","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or derived from tradition. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Communicated from ancestors to descendants orally."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One with traditional beliefs.","Anything that is traditional, conventional, standard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traditional"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tradition","blocks":[{"text":"A tradition is a system of beliefs or behaviors passed down within a group of people or society with symbolic meaning or special significance with origins in the past. A component of cultural expressions and folklore, common examples include holidays or impractical but socially meaningful clothes, but the idea has also been applied to social norms and behaviors such as greetings. Traditions can persist and evolve for thousands of years. The word tradition itself derives from the Latin word tradere literally meaning to transmit, to hand over, to give for safekeeping. While it is reportedly assumed that traditions have an ancient history, many traditions have been invented on purpose, whether it be political or cultural, over short periods of time. Various academic disciplines also use the word in a variety of ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tradition-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/330px-Tradition-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tradition"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg/500px-Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg/1280px-Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg/500px-Indian_historical_Traditional_drama%28_In_stage_performance_-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional dress and arts, such as in  this performance of Traditional Hindi Drama -- the performance of tradition through folklore, reinforces the stories and memory reinforces the concept of tradition, and its importance in local communities.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndian_historical_Traditional_drama(_In_stage_performance_-1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg/500px-Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg/1280px-Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg/500px-Tradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A slametan tradition of a ritual proceeding before Ramadan to honor ancestors and Ramadan in Banyumas, Central Java, Indonesia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATradisi_Unggahan_Bonokeling.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg/500px-Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg/1280px-Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg/500px-Wigilia_potrawy_76.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Holiday celebrations may be passed down as traditions, as is the case with this distinctly Polish Christmas meal, decor with Christmas tree, a tradition since the late 18th and early 19th centuries.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWigilia_potrawy_76.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/GOOD_SHABBES_-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig